  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/72) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello, I noticed the following in the noise reduction tool. When setting the luminance slider to \\+100 \\(and all other sliders at default\\), the preview and the saved file show artefacts with non-raw files. More pronounced with 16-bit tiffs, less with jpg’s \\(but still there\\). Conservative/agressive or RGB/Lab doesn’t change anything. This effect isn’t visible with raw files.\n\n16-bit tiff:\n\n![](https://bitbucket.org/repo/9pArXyE/images/2814234640-NR_16bit.tiff.jpg)\nJpg:\n\n![](https://bitbucket.org/repo/9pArXyE/images/533980099-NR.jpg)\n‌\n",
